Workstream ID: atlas-publication
Title: Repair and verify publication of the current Discovery Atlas
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Make the owner-pushed Atlas the exactly verified public website
Dependencies: discovery-atlas, atlas-progression-redesign, atlas-living-motion
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/26
Purpose: Inspect the owner's pushed revision and actual Pages deployment,
  repair confirmed release blockers, and verify that the published website
  contains the current source-derived Atlas progression and animated interface.
  Preserve the owner's commit, private records and original tracking identities.

Tasks:
  [x] Verify the owner-pushed source and inspect its exact failed Pages run.
  [x] Reproduce the two obsolete Fieldcraft progression-call assertions.
  [x] Update those callers to the EXP-total contract without changing app rules.
  [x] Qualify the repair and update current public-facing release documentation.
  [x] Publish the bounded corrective commit with verified repository attribution.
  [x] Preserve the first successful release and diagnose its one recovered CI test.
  [x] Qualify the explicit stale-review setup wait without changing sync behavior.
  [ ] Verify the exact successful Pages source, required jobs and artifact.
  [ ] Compare hosted files and exercise the real public Atlas in disposable contexts.
  [ ] Close the original completed Atlas items and verify their existing identities.
  [ ] Seal public-safe release evidence and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
  The owner-pushed commit and unrelated work remain intact; no history rewrite.
  A failing deployment is diagnosed from its actual source/jobs/logs, not an
    inference from a clean checkout, local proof or the owner's successful push.
  Tests use snapshot.journey.xp for getWayfinderProgress; discovery count remains
    a separate collection metric. Existing expected outcomes/guards remain.
  Current validation, production build and exact hosted workflow pass without
    skipping checks, increasing retries or relaxing assertions to force success.
  The actual public website matches its successful Pages artifact and supports
    the current Atlas defaults, expeditions, rewards, animation and pause.
  Existing evidence/criteria, backups, tutorial isolation and local records hold.
  Current README/guides accurately describe the released product, retaining
    all four approved illustrations and historical source-bound research receipts.
  No owner browser profile, private report/PDF/context, credential or browser
    backup enters source publication or issue/Project descriptions.
  Preserve original issue/Project/item identities, Kanban and human-owned edits;
    technical deployment, positive owner feedback and measured outcomes differ.
  No extra feature, new service/schedule, workflow bypass or secret provisioning.

